The global spread of the coronavirus has created significant volatility, uncertainty and disruption in healthcare, social and economic infrastructures.
The extent to which the coronavirus pandemic impacts our business, operations and financial results will depend on numerous evolving factors that we may
not be able to accurately predict or plan around, including:
• the duration, volatility and scope of the pandemic;
• governmental, business and individuals’ actions that have been and continue to be taken in response to the pandemic;
• the impact of the pandemic on economic and political activity and actions taken in response;
